{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
They [Dm]came out to the garden when [C]the Passover was through
[Bb]The olive trees were silver and [Dm]the night was cold and blue
He took Peter and the brothers [C]and he walked a little way
[Bb]Then he fell down on his [A]face and he began to pray
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
My Fa[Dm]ther, if it is possi[C]ble, let this cup pass from [Bb]me
Yet not as I will, but as you will
Not my [A]will, but yours be [Dm]done
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He came back to the others and he [C]found them fast asleep
[Bb]Their eyes were heavy with the [Dm]night, too heavy now to keep
So you could not keep watch with me [C]for even one hour?
He [Bb]asked them in the garden while the night [A]held all its power
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Keep watch [Bb]and pray that you may not [C]fall into temptation
[Dm]The spirit is willing, but the [A]flesh is weak
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
An angel came from heaven and [C]it strengthened him to stand
His [Bb]sweat became like drops of blood that [Dm]fell upon the land
He prayed a second time and [C]then he prayed a third
And [Bb]every time he knelt to pray [A]he prayed the same words
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
My Father, if [Bb]this cannot pass unless [Dm]I drink it
[Bb]Your will be done [Dm][Bb][A]
Get up, let us [Dm]go
Look, my betrayer is [C]here
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
My Father, if it [Bb]is possible, let this cup pass from me
Yet not as [A]I will, but as you [Dm]will
Not my will, but yours be done
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Not my will, but yours [Dm]be done
{end_of_verse}
